# Hermes — Project Overview

Hermes is a production-grade, serverless document-processing platform on AWS,
built as a portfolio and learning project. Authoritative docs live in `docs/`:

- Architecture: `docs/architecture.md`
- Technical requirements & quality bar: `docs/technical-requirements.md`
- Features (source of truth): `docs/features.md`
- Decisions: `docs/adr/`
- Step-by-step learning path: `docs/roadmap/`

## Core architecture

- Flow: `API Gateway -> Upload Lambda -> S3 (presigned) -> EventBridge -> SQS ->
  Processing Lambda -> DynamoDB`, read via `Get Document Lambda`.
- Layered/hexagonal per Lambda: `handler -> service -> repository/processor`
  (behind interfaces). Not MVC.
- DynamoDB single-table-light (PK=documentId + SK + 1 GSI).
- Reliability via SQS DLQ + idempotency (conditional writes + Powertools
  Idempotency).

## Stack

TypeScript (strict), AWS Lambda (Node 22), Middy, Zod, AWS SDK v3, Lambda
Powertools, Terraform, LocalStack (dev), Vitest, GitHub Actions. pnpm + Turborepo.

When a decision is significant, add an ADR. Keep `docs/features.md` in sync.
